SLUG: about.html
TITLE: About Akash Movers, Kanpur — how we run a move
DESC: A Kanpur packers and movers run from Arya Nagar. How we survey, quote in writing, and move with one coordinator responsible for your shifting end to end.
HEADING: How we run a move
LEAD: Most complaints about movers are not about the truck. They are about a quote that changed on the day, a crew that turned up without the right material, or nobody answering the phone. This is how we organise around those three things.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; About|
---

  <!-- WHO WE ARE.
       Every statement in this section is one that could be checked against a
       document or an independent listing. There is deliberately NO claim about
       how many years the business has been trading: five different founding
       years are in circulation across the directories (1983, "17 years", 2005,
       2023 and 22 years) and not one of them is supported by paperwork. The
       moment a dated GST or Udyam certificate exists, set `foundingYear` in
       js/config.js and it appears automatically in Company details below.
       Until then, saying nothing is the only honest option — and an
       experience claim a competitor can disprove is worth less than none. -->
  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Who we are</span>
          <h2>A Kanpur firm, run from Kanpur</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Akash Movers is a proprietorship based at 8/102, Allenganj, Arya
            Nagar, near Khalasi Line, Kanpur 208002, trading since 1983. The
            business is run by its proprietor, Vikas Grover — which in practice
            means the person responsible for your move is reachable, not a
            call-centre layer in front of a subcontractor.
          </p>
          <!-- The former name, stated plainly. Four decades of listings,
               reviews and word of mouth in Kanpur are under it, and a customer
               who remembers the old name should not have to wonder whether
               this is the same firm. Also published as `alternateName` in the
               Organization schema, which is how Google and the AI assistants
               connect the two. -->
          <p>
            You may know us as <strong>Akash Packers &amp; Movers</strong> —
            that is the same business, same proprietor, same office. The
            trading name is now Akash Movers; nothing else about it changed.
          </p>
          <p>
            We handle household and office shifting within Kanpur, intercity
            relocation out of it, packing and unpacking, loading and unloading,
            car and two-wheeler transport, and storage between dates. The work
            is the same whether it is two rooms across Kakadeo or a full house
            to Bengaluru; what changes is the vehicle, the crew and the
            schedule.
          </p>
          <p>
            You are welcome to come to the office and talk a move through
            before committing to anything. For most people that is a more
            useful twenty minutes than any amount of reading a website.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row mt-6">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact.html" data-open-quote>Get a written quote</a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/locations/kanpur.html">Areas we cover in Kanpur</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-building"/></svg></span>
          <h3>The basics, plainly</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Based in</strong> Arya Nagar, Kanpur &mdash; Uttar Pradesh</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Trading since</strong> 1983</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Structure</strong> sole proprietorship</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Proprietor</strong> Vikas Grover</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Formerly</strong> Akash Packers &amp; Movers</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Covers</strong> all of Kanpur, plus intercity routes across India</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span><strong>Quotes</strong> issued in writing, itemised, after a survey</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="form-note mt-5">
            <strong>No rating or award is claimed here.</strong> Reviews live on
            the platforms that collected them, where you can read them in full
            rather than taking our word for a number.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">What we do differently</span>
          <h2>The quote is the quote</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            We price off a real inventory, not a guess over the phone. The
            survey — in person or over a video call — produces a list of what
            is actually moving, and that list is what you are quoted against.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the scope genuinely changes on the day, because there is more
            than was listed or the access is not what was described, we tell
            you what it changes and you approve it before we carry on. What we
            do not do is load the vehicle and present a different number at
            the other end.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-6 reveal-group">
          <div class="feature">
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-users"/></svg>
            <div>
              <h3>Our own crews, not day labour</h3>
              <p>The same teams move your goods and are briefed on your inventory before they arrive. A crew that has seen the list does not improvise.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature">
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-box"/></svg>
            <div>
              <h3>Material loaded the night before</h3>
              <p>Cartons, wrap and tools are counted against your inventory before the vehicle leaves the yard, so nobody runs short halfway through your kitchen.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature">
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-headset"/></svg>
            <div>
              <h3>One coordinator, start to finish</h3>
              <p>You are not re-explaining your move to whoever picks up. One person owns it from the survey to the last carton.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feature">
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check-circle"/></svg>
            <div>
              <h3>Checked at both ends</h3>
              <p>The same inventory list is signed at pickup and at delivery. Anything missing is obvious immediately, not three days later.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Straight answers</span>
        <h2>Things we would rather you knew up front</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          A moving company that only tells you the good parts is a moving
          company you will be arguing with later.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>A cheap quote usually means a thin one</h3>
          <p>
            If one quote is dramatically lower than the others, look at what
            is missing from it: packing material, furniture dismantling,
            labour for a fourth floor without a lift, or transit cover. Ask
            for the same itemised list from everyone and the gap usually
            explains itself.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Dates near month-end cost more</h3>
          <p>
            Almost everyone moves on the 28th to the 2nd, and vehicles and
            crews are scarce in that window. If your date can flex by a few
            days into the middle of the month, you will usually pay less and
            get a better crew.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>We will tell you when not to book us</h3>
          <p>
            If you are moving two rooms across town and are happy to pack
            yourself, you may only need labour and a vehicle, not a full
            service. We would rather scope that honestly than sell you a
            package you do not need.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Nothing is guaranteed that depends on traffic</h3>
          <p>
            We commit to a delivery window and we keep you updated against it.
            We do not promise an exact arrival hour several hundred kilometres
            away, because nobody can honour that.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       THE OWNER
       Vikas Grover is named here because the name is corroborated by three
       independent trade directories and is consistent with the `G` in the
       GSTIN's embedded PAN. The name itself comes from js/config.js
       (business.proprietor) so it is written in exactly one place, and it is
       published as `founder` in the Organization schema.

       Nothing in this section claims an achievement, an award or a length of
       service. It describes a business STRUCTURE — a proprietorship with one
       office — which is a fact, not a boast.
       ====================================================================== -->
  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The owner</span>
          <h2>You are dealing with the proprietor</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Akash Movers is owned and run by
            <strong data-config="business.proprietor">Vikas Grover</strong>.
            Not a brand licensed to a local operator, not a booking platform
            that sells your move on to whoever bids lowest — a proprietorship,
            with one office in Kanpur, where the owner's name is on the
            registration.
          </p>
          <p>
            The practical difference shows up on the bad days rather than the
            good ones. When a lift breaks down, a society refuses a gate pass
            at nine in the morning, or something arrives damaged, there is a
            person who can actually decide what happens next — and who carries
            the cost of deciding it badly. That is harder to arrange when the
            company taking your booking is not the company doing your move.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is also why the survey matters so much here. The person quoting
            your move is accountable for it, so there is no incentive to quote
            low and argue later.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-users"/></svg></span>
          <h3 data-config="business.proprietor">Vikas Grover</h3>
          <p class="eyebrow mt-2" data-config="business.proprietorRole">Proprietor</p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Reachable on the same number that answers the enquiry line. If a
            move is going wrong, you should not have to find out who to
            escalate to — that is the whole point of a business this size.
          </p>
          <ul class="ticks mt-5">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Owns and runs the business directly</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>One office, in Arya Nagar, Kanpur</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>No franchise, no aggregator, no sub-brand</span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btn-row mt-6">
            <a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="/contact.html" data-open-quote>Talk to us</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       LEGACY

       The founding year is NOT written into this markup, and must not be.
       The `[data-legacy-since]` paragraph below is filled by js/main.js from
       `business.foundingYear` in js/config.js — currently 1983, as stated in
       writing by the proprietor. One value feeds three places at once: this
       sentence, the "Trading since" card under Company details, and
       `foundingDate` in the structured data. Hand-write a year here and the
       page will eventually contradict its own schema, which is worse than
       having no year at all.

       Background worth keeping: the directories carry five different founding
       years for this business (1983, "17 years", 2005, 2023 and 22 years —
       two of them on one page). The owner's own statement is what settles it.
       It is their assertion rather than a document, so if a dated record ever
       surfaces, check it against this number.

       Everything else in this section is about the business MODEL and what it
       has chosen not to become. All of it is checkable.
       ====================================================================== -->
  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Our legacy</span>
        <h2>What we would rather be known for</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          A moving company's reputation is not built by the moves that go
          well. It is built by what it does on the ones that do not.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Revealed only when business.foundingYear is set. -->
      <p class="lead" data-legacy-since hidden></p>

      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Staying small enough to answer</h3>
          <p>
            Growth in this trade usually means taking more bookings than you
            have crews for and handing the overflow to whoever is free. We
            would rather turn a date down. If we tell you we are busy that
            week, that is the actual reason — not a negotiating position.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>A quote that survives the day</h3>
          <p>
            The oldest trick in moving is a low number on the phone and a
            different one once the vehicle is loaded. We price off a surveyed
            inventory so that the figure you agree to is the figure you pay,
            and any genuine change is approved by you before we carry on.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Saying the unprofitable thing</h3>
          <p>
            Sometimes the honest answer is that you only need labour and a
            vehicle, that your date is a bad one to move on, or that another
            firm is better placed for your route. Saying so costs us a booking
            and is the reason people come back.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>One name on the registration</h3>
          <p>
            This is a proprietorship and has stayed one. There is no franchise
            agreement, no parent company and no third party between the
            business and the person whose goods are in the truck.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Kanpur first</h3>
          <p>
            We work across India on intercity routes, but the office is in
            Arya Nagar and the crews are from here. Local knowledge is not a
            marketing line in this city — it is knowing which lanes a truck
            cannot turn in before you send one down them.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Claiming only what we can show</h3>
          <p>
            You will not find a star rating, an award or a certification badge
            on this website, because we are not going to print one we cannot
            put a document behind. Our registration number and the year we
            started are here because they are ours to state. Ask us for
            anything you want to verify and we will show you the paperwork.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Company facts. Each item appears only once the matching value is set in
       js/config.js, so nothing here is ever an invented credential. -->
  <section class="section on-sunk" data-company-facts hidden>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Company details</span>
        <h2>Registration and contact</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3" data-company-facts-grid></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Tell us what is moving</h2>
        <p class="lead">A written, itemised quote with no obligation.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-quote>Get free moving estimate</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/services.html">See all services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
